#: ../../source/plugins/index.rst:5
msgid "Plugins"
msgstr "插件"

#: ../../source/plugins/index.rst:20
msgid ""
"Most of what PartCAD can do, PartCAD does not hard-code. A **plugin** is a "
"declaration in somebody's ``partcad.yaml`` saying which script does a job, "
"what its sandbox needs, and what it produces -- and a package that imports "
"it can then use that job as if PartCAD had always had it."
msgstr ""
"PartCAD 所能做的大部分事情，都不是 PartCAD 硬编码进去的。**插件** 就是某人 ``partcad.yaml`` "
"中的一段声明，它说明由哪个脚本来干某项活、它的沙箱需要什么，以及它产出什么 -- 而导入它的包随后就可以使用这项活，仿佛 PartCAD "
"一直就有它一样。"

#: ../../source/plugins/index.rst:24
msgid ""
"That is why the list of formats PartCAD reads, the applications it opens a "
"file in, the solvers it asks and the simulators it runs are not fixed: each "
"is a section a package writes, and the wheel ships few of them. A plugin is "
"an ordinary package, versioned and imported like any other, so **adding a "
"capability to PartCAD is publishing a package rather than changing "
"PartCAD**."
msgstr ""
"正因如此，PartCAD 读得了哪些格式、它用哪些应用程序打开文件、它去问哪些求解器、它跑哪些仿真器，都不是固定的：每一项都是某个包所写的一个小节，而 "
"wheel 本身只附带其中少数几个。插件就是一个普通的包，像其他包一样做版本管理、被导入，所以 **给 PartCAD "
"添加一项能力，是去发布一个包，而不是去改 PartCAD**。"

#: ../../source/plugins/index.rst:29
msgid ""
"A plugin's script runs in a :doc:`sandbox </maintenance/sandboxes>`, which "
"is what lets it bring its own dependencies -- a mesh library, a solver, a "
"vendor's SDK -- without those reaching your package or PartCAD itself. What "
"it produces is cached under the environment that produced it, the way "
"everything else is."
msgstr ""
"插件的脚本运行在一个 :doc:`沙箱 </maintenance/sandboxes>` 中，正是这一点让它可以自带依赖 -- "
"一个网格库、一个求解器、某厂商的 SDK -- 而这些东西不会波及到你的包或 PartCAD "
"本身。它所产出的东西会按产出它的那个环境来缓存，与其他一切一样。"

